# Build context exclusions.
#
# .env is the important one: without it, real credentials are copied into an image
# layer and persist there even if a later layer deletes the file. Anyone who can pull
# the image can read them back out with `docker history`.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local virtualenv — the image builds its own; copying this in would also break it,
# since the paths inside are absolute to the host.
.venv

.git
.github
.gitignore

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage

.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Not needed at runtime. README.md is deliberately NOT excluded: pyproject.toml
# declares `readme = "README.md"`, so the uv_build backend fails without it.
Makefile
docker/
